What is printed when demonstrating the Liskov Substitution Principle with polymorphic assignment?

```java
class Instrument {
    String play() { return "Note"; }
}
class Flute extends Instrument {
    String play() { return "Melody"; }
}
public class Main {
    static void audition(Instrument inst) {
        System.out.print(inst.play() + " ");
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Instrument i = new Instrument();
        Flute f = new Flute();
        audition(i);
        audition(f);
    }
}
```
